L000562.text:
We had a significant victory for labor rights in Congress this week! I’m proud that we passed the Faster Labor Contracts Act with the support of the @AFLCIO, @Teamsters, the Laborers’ International Union of North America, @TheIronworkers, the Transport Workers Union of America, and our other partners in the American labor movement.

This bipartisan bill ensures that bad-faith employers cannot simply subvert workers who have formed a new union by endlessly stalling negotiations on a first contract. In the event of any delay of more than 10 days, a contract dispute will be promptly referred to a mediator and, if necessary, arbitration, to ensure that workers are fully able to exercise their collective bargaining rights and secure change in the workplace.

@Labor_Caucus

